{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/484967-narnia-changeling-what","id":484967,"title":"Narnia + Changeling = ...What?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-18T18:33:50-07:00","id":484967,"title":"Narnia + Changeling = ...What?","content":"Anyhoo, I've been [REDACTED TO PROTECT SOURCES]<br /> <br /> This ain't about that, not entirely. Rather, it was mentioned at one point there's a theme of planetary symbolism throughout the books, with Saturn, the symbol of old age and cynicism, being the ultimate enemy. Which is, I realized, kind of the opposite of the point in Lost; Saturn, as old age and maturity, is actually an okay planet, as it both recognizes that innocence was spoiled and there's nothing to be done. Time to make a better adulthood.<br /> <br /> So, I was thinking-a group of bookhound Lost found a new freehold and decide, &quot;You know what? The Fae aren't exactly the most modern-thinking beings in the world. Let's model ourselves after a modern fairy tale!&quot; Volia, a freehold where the nobility takes after Narnia characters (not precisely, obviously: The &quot;Jadis&quot; is the Winter Queen, and making her Season eternal is something she's aware is a very bad idea).<br /> <br /> Good idea? What kind of stories, you think, will arise from that, particularly when the Keepers<i> do</i> catch on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-19-2015, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T18:44:30-07:00","id":484993,"title":"","content":"I might be aware of the deconstructions you're aware of. I remember reading a few essays discussing how horrifying it would be to be dragged into Narnia by magic. Honestly, this makes me want to write up a scenario with Susan and Edmund as the Changelings and Aslan and Jadis as the Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T11:42:24-07:00","id":485524,"title":"","content":"If you don't want people going back and looking at your sources (in this case the deconstruction) then you should just not mention them. Seriously, that whole first paragraph serves no purpose except to make me google the subject to figure out who you're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T14:09:57-07:00","id":485702,"title":"","content":"...You're probably right.<br /> <br /> D'oh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T19:15:39-07:00","id":485903,"title":"","content":"Wait, what was redacted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T19:32:10-07:00","id":485932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/484967-narnia-changeling-what?p=485903#post485903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what was redacted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sources.<br /> <br /> I though a nice request to not post mine's identity would be enough to deter the trolls they've dealt with (not saying you are, I am just protecting them from hypothetical trolls) but helel pointed out I put out enough information in my backstory to reasonably google them.<br /> <br /> So my little backstory is gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T22:18:33-07:00","id":490210,"title":"","content":"You're talking about the 2e system of setting up your own Courts, right? In that case, I'd be inclined to pattern the Courts after the four Kings and Queens of Narnia: Peter, Susan, Edmund, and Lucy. That said, you might want to go even more recent in your source material, and do something like Griffindor, Hufflepuff, Slytherin, and Ravenclaw as your Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=